The `arp_packet_match()` function (lines 107-207) contains the vulnerable construct. Specifically, at lines 155-160, the code unconditionally assumes a standard ARP packet layout with both source and target hardware addresses:


src_devaddr = arpptr;
arpptr += dev->addr_len;
memcpy(&src_ipaddr, arpptr, sizeof(u32));
arpptr += sizeof(u32);
tgt_devaddr = arpptr;
arpptr += dev->addr_len;
memcpy(&tgt_ipaddr, arpptr, sizeof(u32));


This pointer arithmetic assumes the packet contains: source hardware address (dev->addr_len bytes), source IP address (4 bytes), target hardware address (dev->addr_len bytes), and target IP address (4 bytes). However, IEEE1394 (FireWire) ARP packets per RFC 2734 omit the target hardware address field, causing `tgt_devaddr` to point to incorrect data and `tgt_ipaddr` to be read from the wrong offset. The function performs comparisons on these incorrectly-extracted values (lines 165-169), leading to potential out-of-bounds reads. There is no check for the hardware type (ar_hrd) or packet length validation to handle variable ARP packet formats, so the vulnerability is not fixed in this initial commit.

The `arp_packet_match()` function (lines 109-213) contains the vulnerable construct. It unconditionally assumes a standard ARP packet layout with both source and target hardware addresses. Specifically, lines 161-167 show the problematic pointer arithmetic:


src_devaddr = arpptr;
arpptr += dev->addr_len;
memcpy(&src_ipaddr, arpptr, sizeof(u32));
arpptr += sizeof(u32);
tgt_devaddr = arpptr;
arpptr += dev->addr_len;
memcpy(&tgt_ipaddr, arpptr, sizeof(u32));


This code assumes the ARP payload layout is: [src_devaddr][src_ipaddr][tgt_devaddr][tgt_ipaddr]. However, RFC 2734 specifies that IEEE1394 (FireWire) ARP packets omit the target hardware address field, making the actual layout: [src_devaddr][src_ipaddr][tgt_ipaddr]. The code reads `tgt_devaddr` and `tgt_ipaddr` from incorrect offsets in IEEE1394 packets, causing out-of-bounds reads and potential memory corruption. The function lacks any check for the hardware type (ar_hrd) or address length (ar_hln) to handle variable ARP packet formats. No fix is present in this initial commit.
